# QEMU / KVM / virt-manager
# "opengl" isn't a real qemu flag - the one that actually gives you GPU-
# accelerated virtio-gpu display is "virgl". qemu_user_targets_x86_64 is for
# running foreign x86_64 binaries via binfmt on a non-x86_64 host - not
# relevant here, so it's dropped. libvirt was missing entirely; virt-manager
# needs it, and virt-manager's own flags are just gui+policykit (spice/gtk
# were never valid on virt-manager - spice/usbredir belong on qemu itself).
app-emulation/qemu spice usbredir virtfs virgl sdl gtk vnc pipewire alsa qemu_softmmu_targets_x86_64
app-emulation/libvirt qemu libvirtd virt-network fuse nfs numa udev policykit
app-emulation/virt-manager gui policykit

